IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il44-nouns`

-- Row il-44. THE CROSS-REFERENCES OF SECTION 12A1(a) OF THE ENTRY INTO ISRAEL LAW, 5712-1952, as typed values, and the days that bear on them.
-- A citation is encoded as TWO descriptions: what the citing words say the cited section is about, and what that section of that instrument is about. A test compares them.
-- Where they differ, the citation does not point at what it says it does. That is the one defect of this row, D1; the six references after it are sound, and are its controls.
--
-- WHAT THE QUOTED LINES ARE.
--   `src:N |`   a line of the Entry into Israel Law in the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation, revision 3037272 (UNOFFICIAL; CONSOLIDATION-ONLY), expanded mechanically from the deposit by tools/srcquote.py.
--   `ext:[ordinance] N |` and `ext:[law1982] N |`   a line of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (revision 3037798) and of the Criminal Procedure Law [Consolidated Version] (revision 3079022),
--     expanded mechanically from the deposits by tools/extquote.py. Both are UNOFFICIAL: everything they say about a section's content is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
--   `ext:[SH ..., read from the page image] |`   Hebrew transcribed by the encoder from the page image of the Knesset's PDF of Sefer HaChukim, deposited in `../../registers/source-bundle/page-images/`.
--     These lines are not copied mechanically; tools/hebcheck.py skips them, and NOTES.md section 12 says how they were checked.
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO. It does not type every citation of the Law. It types the seven below: the six that section 12A1(a) makes to the two Criminal Procedure instruments, and one from section 12(b)(2),
-- which cites the same section 32 of the Ordinance and was enacted on the same page of the same instrument that last touched section 12A1(a).

§ `Cross-references of section 12A1`

-- The test of a single citation: do the citing words and the target say the same thing?
GIVEN c IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation points at what it says` MEANS c's `the citing words say that section is about` EQUALS c's `that section of that instrument is about`

-- The test of two citations: if both give the same section number, do they name the same instrument?
GIVEN a IS A `A cross-reference`
      b IS A `A cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two citations name the same instrument for the same section number` MEANS
    (NOT (a's `the section number the citing words give` EQUALS b's `the section number the citing words give`))
    OR (a's `the citing words use the short name of` EQUALS b's `the citing words use the short name of`)

-- THE DEFECT, D1. Section 12A1(a)(2)(b): "the court that convicted a foreign resident ... shall order forfeiture of the vehicle seized under section 32 of the Criminal Procedure LAW".
-- Paragraph (1) of the same subsection names the same seizure as "section 32 of the Criminal Procedure ORDINANCE". Section 32 of the LAW is repealed (SH 1592, section 41).
-- src:300 | (א) חוק סדר הדין הפלילי [נוסח משולב], התשמ״ב–1982 (בחוק זה – חוק סדר הדין הפלילי), ופקודת סדר הדין הפלילי (מעצר וחיפוש) [נוסח חדש], התשכ״ט–1969 (בחוק זה – פקודת סדר הדין הפלילי), יחולו על תושב זר החשוד בעבירה לפי סעיף 12(א)(1) בשינויים אלה:
-- src:301 | (1) על אף הוראות סעיף 128 לחוק סדר הדין הפלילי, יחולו הוראות סעיף 130 שבו גם על נאשם שהוזמן לתחילת המשפט ובלבד שבהזמנה למשפט הוזהר כי בית המשפט יהיה רשאי לדונו שלא בפניו ולהורות על חילוט רכב שנתפס לפי סעיף 32 לפקודת סדר הדין הפלילי, אם לא יתייצב;
-- src:304 | (ב) על אף הוראות סעיף 39 שבה, בית המשפט שהרשיע תושב זר בעבירה לפי סעיף 12(א)(1), יורה, נוסף על כל עונש, על חילוט הרכב שנתפס לפי סעיף 32 לחוק סדר הדין הפלילי [note: [צ״ל: לפקודת סדר הדין הפלילי]] אף אם לא התייצב למשפטו, אלא אם כן החליט, מטעמים מיוחדים שיירשמו, שלא לעשות כן;
