§ `Days`

-- The repeal of section 32 of the Law was published in Sefer HaChukim 1592 on 12 May 1996 and took effect "at the end of one year from its publication" (section 48 of that Law).
-- Which day that is depends on how the Interpretation Law counts the year, and this row did not read it (fork C1 in NOTES.md): the first day in force is taken to be 12 May 1997 or 13 May 1997, both kept as values.
-- ext:[SH 1592 p.352, footer, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 1592, כ"ג באייר התשנ"ו, 12.5.1996
-- ext:[SH 1592 p.352, section 48, read from the page image] | תחילתו של חוק זה בתום שנה מפרסומו.
`the day Sefer HaChukim 1592 was published` MEANS Date 12 5 1996
`the earliest first day of force of the repeal` MEANS Date 12 5 1997
`the latest first day of force of the repeal` MEANS Date 13 5 1997

-- ext:[SH 1808 p.568, footer, read from the page image] | ספר חוקים 1808, י"ח באלול התשס"א, 6.9.2001
`the day Sefer HaChukim 1808 was published` MEANS Date 6 9 2001

-- ext:[SH 3441 p.725, footer, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 3441, י"ז בתמוז התשפ"ה, 13.7.2025
`the day Sefer HaChukim 3441 was published` MEANS Date 13 7 2025
